### =====================================================================
### inventory-service - ready-to-run requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8106, so we send the X-User-* / X-Store-Id headers
### ourselves (normally the API gateway adds them from the JWT).
###
### Seed data (docs/seed-data.md), low-stock threshold 5 everywhere:
###   store 1 Fresh Mart   (vendor1 = user 3): products 1-10 and 17
###       7 Amul Butter = 3 units (LOW), 17 Mango Alphonso = 0 (OUT OF STOCK)
###   store 2 Green Basket (vendor2 = user 6): products 11-16
###       13 Pomegranate = 0 (OUT OF STOCK), 14 Nandini Curd = 4 (LOW)
###
### Creating the FIRST stock for a product calls product-read-service (port 8105)
### to check that the product belongs to the vendor's store.
### Requests 15-16 put the seed values back.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8106


### 1. INTERNAL: publish the current stock of every product as StockChanged events.
#    Run once after the first start: the seed rows were inserted by SQL, so no event exists for them yet.
#    Afterwards product-read-service shows stock in search.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/inventory/stock-snapshot


### 2. VENDOR (store 1): my stock, page 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory?page=0&size=20
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 3. VENDOR (store 1): only items that need restocking -> products 7 and 17
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory?lowStockOnly=true
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 4. VENDOR (store 1): stock of Tomato (product 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/1
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 5. VENDOR (store 1): counted the shelf - Tomato is now 100 units, alert at 10
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantityOnHand": 100,
  "lowStockThreshold": 10
}


### 6. VENDOR (store 1): 20 units of Amul Butter arrived -> 23, no longer low
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/7/additions
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantity": 20
}


### 7. VENDOR (store 1): Amul Butter down to 2 -> low again: publishes StockChanged AND LowStockDetected
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/7
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantityOnHand": 2
}


### 8. VENDOR (store 1): product 11 belongs to store 2 -> 404 (as if it did not exist)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/11
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 9. VENDOR (store 1): unknown product -> 404 from the product check in product-read-service
#    (503 if product-read-service is not running)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/999
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantityOnHand": 10
}


### 10. VENDOR (store 1): invalid numbers -> 400 with one error per field
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantityOnHand": -1,
  "lowStockThreshold": -5
}


### 11. VENDOR without an approved store (user 10, no X-Store-Id) -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory
X-User-Id: 10
X-User-Role: VENDOR


### 12. ADMIN: low stock across ALL stores -> 7, 13, 14, 17
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/inventory?lowStockOnly=true
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 13. ADMIN: all stock of store 2, highest quantity first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/inventory?storeId=2&sort=quantityOnHand,desc
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 14. INTERNAL: stock of Pomegranate (product 13) - used by other services
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/inventory/products/13


### 15. RESET: Tomato back to the seed values (120 units, threshold 5)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantityOnHand": 120,
  "lowStockThreshold": 5
}


### 16. RESET: Amul Butter back to the seed value (3 units)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/7
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "quantityOnHand": 3
}
